  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "SLN admits negative life, evaluates x87-stored (cost - salvage) / life, and flushes only the published quotient to +0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, SLN(cost, salvage, life) admits negative or fractional cost, salvage, and nonzero life (returning #DIV/0! only when life == 0), evaluates RN53(RN64((cost - salvage) / life)) while retaining subnormal differences before division, and flushes only the final quotient to +0.0 if subnormal. All 1,205 full-bank SLN rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20430 (1,205/1,205 full-bank and 120/120 pinned SLN rows) and 16.0.20527.20088 in f3_financial (row 10) and prefix_metadata (row 388).",
